<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong>22 November 2025</p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>LONELYPARTNER.COM</strong> (“the Platform”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses, and protects
your personal data.  
We operate from the Netherlands and follow the GDPR/AVG and all applicable EU privacy laws.
Our goal is to protect your privacy while providing a safe and enjoyable experience.
</p>

<h2>2. Data We Collect</h2>
<p>We collect the minimum data necessary to operate the Platform responsibly, including:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Account Data:</strong> Email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Age Verification Data:</strong> Confirmation of being 18+; optional ID verification where legally required.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP address, device information, browser type, activity logs.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment Data:</strong> Processed by secure third-party providers; we do not store payment card numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>Communications:</strong> Messages and support interactions.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Live Camera Sessions</h2>
<p>
Peer-to-peer sessions are designed to be private.  
We do not monitor, access, or record live video or audio except in situations where:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>a session is flagged for abuse prevention or investigation,</li>
    <li>a user reports misconduct, or</li>
    <li>we are required to comply with a lawful request.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
<p>We process data under the following GDPR bases:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> (registration, optional verification).</li>
    <li><strong>Contract</strong> (providing access to the Platform).</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> (age restrictions, safety, compliance).</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> (security, fraud prevention).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. How We Use Your Data</h2>
<p>We use personal data to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Provide and operate the Platform.</li>
    <li>Ensure safety, fraud prevention, and abuse detection.</li>
    <li>Support payment and billing functions.</li>
    <li>Respond to user requests and customer support inquiries.</li>
    <li>Improve Platform stability, performance, and reliability.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
<p>We may share data with:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Trusted service providers (hosting, payments, security).</li>
    <li>Law enforcement, only when legally required.</li>
</ul>
<p>We never sell personal data.</p>

<h2>7. Cookies & Analytics</h2>
<p>
We use essential cookies for login and platform functionality.  
Analytics cookies are used only with user consent, in line with EU cookie regulations.
</p>

<h2>8. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
<p>
Under EU law, you have the right to:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Access your personal data.</li>
    <li>Request correction or deletion of your data.</li>
    <li>Request restriction of processing.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent at any time.</li>
    <li>Receive a copy of your data (portability).</li>
    <li>Lodge a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens).</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
<p>
We retain your data only as long as necessary for legal compliance or to provide service functionality.
Inactive accounts may be deleted after a reasonable retention period.
</p>

<h2>10. Security Measures</h2>
<p>
We employ encryption, access controls, secure hosting, and active monitoring to protect personal data.
While we work to safeguard your information, no system is completely risk-free.
</p>

<h2>11. Children’s Privacy</h2>
<p>
The Platform is strictly 18+. We do not knowingly collect data from minors.
If we become aware of an underage user, we will remove the account and comply with reporting obligations.
</p>

<h2>12. International Transfers</h2>
<p>
If data is transferred outside the EEA, we use GDPR-approved safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs).
</p>

<h2>13. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>
We may update this Policy to reflect changes in law or service improvements.
Significant updates will be communicated to users.
</p>

<h2>14. Contact Information</h2>
<p>
For privacy questions or GDPR requests, you can reach us at:  
<strong>support@lonleypartner.com</strong>
</p>

